  "summary": "Looks good \u2014 a minimal happy-path unit test for `slug()` that matches the current implementation.\n\nThe new `tests/test_slug.py` asserts that leading/trailing whitespace is stripped, the string is lowercased, and internal spaces become hyphens (`\" Hello World \"` \u2192 `hello-world`). That is exactly what `utils/slug.py` does today (`strip().lower().replace(\" \", \"-\")`), so the assertion is correct.\n\nCoverage is intentionally thin (one case). That is acceptable for a smoke test of this one-liner; broader edge cases (multi-space runs, empty input, punctuation) would be nice follow-ups if `slug()` grows real consumers and a contract.\n\n**Recommendation:** approve",
